From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: pas: keep handover masked on attach

The one-shot handover fix tracks the IRQ enable state. Freedom's Baldur
attach path bypasses that tracking with raw enable_irq()/disable_irq().
Attach has not acquired proxy resources, so it must not invoke the
handover callback that releases them. Keep this IRQ masked on attach;
normal prepare/unprepare manage it for a subsequent real boot cycle.

This follows the upstream review: SMP2P implements software masking and
does not latch a handover edge while masked. Preserve Freedom's other
attach checks and fallback-to-start behavior.

Link: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/07/31/1411
Applies-after: bb7c5d6f5b41d192fa81ce404e463f5d3ce70cb3
Signed-off-by: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
---

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -518,9 +518,7 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	pas->q6v5.handover_issued = true;
-	/* TB323FU attaches with the handover IRQ unmasked. */
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
-		enable_irq(pas->q6v5.handover_irq);
+	/* No proxy resources were acquired on attach; keep handover masked. */
 
 	pas->q6v5.running = true;
 	ret = irq_get_irqchip_state(pas->q6v5.fatal_irq,
@@ -566,8 +564,6 @@
 	pas->rproc->state = RPROC_OFFLINE;
 	ret = -EINVAL;
 disable_running:
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
-		disable_irq(pas->q6v5.handover_irq);
 	pas->q6v5.running = false;
 
 	return ret;
